        "{\"event\":{\"at\":\"2026-11-03T21:04:38.036Z\",\"kind\":\"decision.recorded\",\"payload\":{\"adr\":\"ADR-2\",\"alternatives\":\"Plain `^export\\\\s+` strip: rejected, it changes the meaning of an existing `export = x` line (key `export`) and `\\\\s` differs between JS and PHP on Unicode whitespace. Accepting `export` with no following blank: rejected, `exporter=3` and `export=1` are ordinary keys. Doing JS first and PHP later: rejected by ADR-1.\",\"rationale\":\"Lines written as `export KEY=value` (a shell habit) read as `KEY=value`. The prefix is `export` followed by spaces or tabs, removed only when the next character is neither `=` nor a blank, so a line that already meant a key named `export` (`export = x`, `export=1`) keeps its meaning instead of becoming `= x` and being skipped. The same pattern, `^export[ \\\\t]+(?=[^= \\\\t])`, is used in `packages/js` and `packages/php` (ADR-1), and with `[ \\\\t]` rather than `\\\\s` so the two languages cannot differ on Unicode whitespace. Tests in both packages cover the prefix, tab/multi-space/indented forms, and the keys that merely start with `export`.\",\"title\":\"EnvAccessor strips a leading `export` + blanks only when a key follows, in both packages\"},\"run\":\"01a1a33a-115d-7000-9e0f-c2c395abca6c\",\"signerFp\":\"8418f7fd8cbfa1df17678d227fbbf095121f987b4fea51815b056ce54af0b878\",\"subject\":\"01a1a33a-6e88-7000-af7e-9275d351f2f7\",\"v\":1,\"which\":\"claude-code\",\"who\":\"mnid:1c8d488d74c49d51bd5e34c2ed5f07f51a42ba58c7b9b5674e459ef293324fee\"},\"link\":{\"hash\":\"6804a9ae174b5dfac5d13c11a5f7f5927ba237ea04b88f98573106493681af54\",\"prev\":\"04530968ea1f4a4451f1aed50d612c605f4acfc7cdac599a9df22f6ef754d0c6\",\"seq\":3,\"tail\":\"8418f7fd8cbfa1df17678d227fbbf095121f987b4fea51815b056ce54af0b878-5bd959e37a3afaf1d76876fc170c85d3\"}}",
